  "rejection_groups": [
    {
      "body": "system.forbiddenDependenciesRegexes is set by each module to name what should have left. It caught #3 (nixos-rebuild still present), #20 and #47 (systemd-minimal had more holders), #52 (elfutils had a third holder) and #57 (krb5 had two more referrers). Writing the guard for what you hope leaves, rather than what you know leaves, is what makes it useful.",
      "count": 4,
      "name": "The guard did its job"
    },
    {
      "body": "Wrong build phase, an unasserted string replacement that silently matched nothing, a measurement that compared only closures, an image that failed to build and was logged as a 100% saving, an integer interpolated into a string, and a mkForce that removed more than it meant to. Each produced a protocol change; see \u00a76.",
      "count": 6,
      "name": "The lab's own defects"
    },
    {
      "body": "A trimmed kernel config derails nixpkgs' make config. Dropping the module tree needs ena, af_packet, fuse and configfs force-loaded in the initrd and the firewall off. An auto-sized image with no slack left growpart nothing to grow into.",
      "count": 5,
      "name": "Genuinely too far"
    }
  ],
